Packed `Deserialize` derives now compile and run with `deserialize_in_place` enabled. `cd test_suite && cargo +nightly test --features unstable` passed, including the new regression tests and the existing suite.

`#[repr(packed)]` fields can be misaligned, so the derive no longer builds `&mut self.place.field` for them. That pattern is both rejected as E0793 and aborted at runtime on this nightly when the reference is actually unaligned. Packed fields are deserialized into a temporary and assigned by value. Other structs still use `InPlaceSeed`.

Files changed:

- `serde_derive/src/de/struct_.rs` — in-place map deserialization for named packed structs
- `serde_derive/src/de.rs` — in-place sequence deserialization, which tuple structs use
- `serde_derive/src/de/tuple.rs` — packed newtype structs
- `test_suite/tests/test_derive_deserialize_packed.rs` — regression coverage for `#[repr(C, packed)]` and `#[repr(packed)]`, including `deserialize_in_place`The nightly test suite finished successfully. `cargo +nightly test --features unstable` in `test_suite` passed, including the packed-struct regression tests.
